00:01:31,145 --> 00:01:32,845
So first, bracketing.

28
00:01:32,845 --> 00:01:39,825
A market is said to be bracketing when it exhibits two-way trade between buyers and sellers.

29
00:01:39,825 --> 00:01:44,430
Now, as you can see, a very basic example is what we have on the right.

30
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:47,300
Let's first look at the handwritten drawing.

31
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:53,275
As you can see, the market is bracketing between what we like to call support and resistance.

32
00:01:53,275 --> 00:01:55,045
Now, what I do want to point out,

33
00:01:55,045 --> 00:01:57,074
guys, is when I refer to

34
00:01:57,074 --> 00:02:00,117
support or resistance, I don't necessarily mean, you know,

35
00:02:00,117 --> 00:02:05,189
at support, buyers are buying the market or at resistance, sellers are selling the market.

36
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:06,733
I merely mean, this

37
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:09,819
is the point where either sellers are stepping

38
00:02:09,819 --> 00:02:15,219
into resistance or buyers are looking to take profits at those same resistance areas.

39
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,920
So, this is what we mean by bracketing.

40
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:24,410
It's when a market starts to trade between two pivots and it respects those pivots and keeps bouncing between them.

41
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:28,142
Then, buyers initiate buying at lower prices near

42
00:02:28,142 --> 00:02:31,874
the bottom of the bracket and will continue

43
00:02:31,874 --> 00:02:38,405
to show initiative until they begin to run into responsive sellers at higher prices.

44
00:02:38,405 --> 00:02:42,165
At this point, buyers will no longer be initiative.

45
00:02:42,165 --> 00:02:47,210
Once prices reach the top of the bracket, sellers will become slightly less responsive.

46
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,818
Why? Because prices are

47
00:02:48,818 --> 00:02:51,231
advertised at a premium and they

48
00:02:51,231 --> 00:02:56,459
