00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:47,165
So, that's the important thing to understand.

242
00:14:47,165 --> 00:14:49,855
If price exploration does not have force

243
00:14:49,855 --> 00:14:52,545
and volume, then the expectation is that

244
00:14:52,545 --> 00:14:56,004
price will be pulled back toward the value area.

245
00:14:56,005 --> 00:15:00,215
So, important you understand, you know, this basic concept.

246
00:15:00,215 --> 00:15:02,924
Now, once the auction is underway,

247
00:15:02,924 --> 00:15:05,633
rather than attempting to predict future

248
00:15:05,633 --> 00:15:10,148
prices, we instead observe as the market discovers future prices.

249
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,435
So, so crucial.

250
00:15:11,435 --> 00:15:13,095
I see so many younger traders,

251
00:15:13,095 --> 00:15:15,309
you know, looking at a chart, and they

252
00:15:15,309 --> 00:15:17,246
look at a chart from the perspective

253
00:15:17,246 --> 00:15:19,183
of where have we come from and,

254
00:15:19,183 --> 00:15:27,487
you know, where are we likely to stop at a, you know, given future date. They don't... they're almost looking at the market and trying to preempt what the story

255
00:15:27,490 --> 00:15:32,975
might be, as opposed to, you know, living in the present and, you know, trading the story as it's occurring.

256
00:15:32,975 --> 00:15:38,190
Now, I'm not suggesting that, you know, going counter-trend the markets is a bad thing.

257
00:15:38,190 --> 00:15:40,313
What I am suggesting is that there

258
00:15:40,313 --> 00:15:42,436
is a time and a place to

259
00:15:42,436 --> 00:15:45,469
both go with the market and go against the market.

260
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:51,040
And that's why we spend a lot of time, you know, developing our strategies based on objective analysis,

261
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:54,450
because that's going to help us, you know, take on trade opportunities.

262
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:56,663
Not that we're guessing or not

263
00:15:56,663 --> 00:15:59,614
that we're thinking where a market might do

264
00:15:59,614 --> 00:16:02,565
something, but rather, you know, we're making good

265
00:16:02,565 --> 00:16:06,623
educated decisions based on factual information provided by the volume profiles.

266
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:09,331
So, as traders, we continually assess

267
00:16:09,331 --> 00:16:12,940
the force and the health of the auction

268
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:16,549
process in order to identify asymmetrical opportunities that

269
00:16:16,549 --> 00:16:22,413
can provide optimal trade location and, more importantly, trade location with less risk.

270
00:16:22,415 --> 00:16:24,252
So, ideally, in an ideal

271
00:16:24,252 --> 00:16:26,823
world situation, what we're looking for, if

272
00:16:26,823 --> 00:16:29,394
we're a momentum trader, we're looking to

273
00:16:29,394 --> 00:16:33,068
be momentum traders when there's a high probability for momentum.

274
00:16:34,130 --> 00:16:35,423
Equally, we're looking to

275
00:16:35,423 --> 00:16:38,009
be sort of almost, you know, not necessarily

276
00:16:38,009 --> 00:16:40,595
fade traders, but we're looking to go counter

277
00:16:40,595 --> 00:16:43,181
trend when there's a lack of momentum, which

278
00:16:43,181 --> 00:16:47,060
is suggestive of a high probability, you know, trade with less risk.

279
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:54,295
So, that is the crux of it, guys, is finding the optimal strategy based on the conditioning of the market.

280
00:16:54,295 --> 00:16:55,790
Now, just in the charts there,

281
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:58,590
as you can see, you know, we're talking about positive and negative skew.

282
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:01,086
So, what I'm trying to illustrate to you

283
00:17:01,086 --> 00:17:03,582
there is that when there is positive skew,

284
00:17:03,582 --> 00:17:07,327
you know, when there's, you know, non-symmetrical type markets, that is when

285
00:17:07,327 --> 00:17:11,072
there's a higher probability or a lean for the markets to continue

286
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:19,187
moving in, not necessarily an aggressive trending manner, but at least moving in, you know, there's a high probability to either move up or move down.

287
00:17:19,190 --> 00:17:22,494
And that's what I'm trying to illustrate is if you

288
00:17:22,494 --> 00:17:25,798
can identify when there's a high probability to move up

289
00:17:25,798 --> 00:17:29,102
or down versus when there's a high likelihood we're just

290
00:17:29,102 --> 00:17:35,379
going to keep balancing, then you can employ some very effective strategies and you can reduce your ultimate risk.

291
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:44,330
So, note, a bracketed market has already confirmed auctioning on both sides, whilst bracketing is still busy confirming.

292
00:17:44,330 --> 00:17:48,765
The trade strategies used will vary in both instances.

293
00:17:48,765 --> 00:17:55,270
In a bracketed market, one can be passive on entry as other influential timeframes are responsive,

294
00:17:55,270 --> 00:17:58,151
where a market that is trying to bracket

295
00:17:58,151 --> 00:18:01,032
has a slightly skewed risk as we are

296
00:18:01,032 --> 00:18:04,994
seeing responsive price response, but also initiative from the trending timeframe.

297
00:18:04,995 --> 00:18:10,520
Therefore, we take on more risk pre-empting a bracketing market than a bracketed market.

298
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,630
So, all I'm trying to say to you is very simple.

299
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:16,369
If a market has established itself as a bracketing market,

300
00:18:16,369 --> 00:18:20,108
in other words, we have clear areas where, you know,

301
00:18:20,108 --> 00:18:23,847
we're finding that there's resistance, you know, for buyers to

302
00:18:23,847 --> 00:18:26,838
buy higher or initiate higher and sellers respond.

303
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:32,095
And then equally on the flip side, you know, sellers, you know, initiated higher prices and then,

304
00:18:32,095 --> 00:18:33,750
you know, buyers responded lower prices.

305
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:37,735
So, if there's clear defined bracketing already,

306
00:18:37,735 --> 00:18:40,374
then as traders we want to initiate strategies

307
00:18:40,374 --> 00:18:43,013
where we are a little bit more passive

308
00:18:43,013 --> 00:18:45,652
and we allow the market to come and

309
00:18:45,652 --> 00:18:51,589
tag us and fill us in and we respond to those higher prices and to those low prices.

310
00:18:51,590 --> 00:18:58,225
However, if a market is still trying to bracket, it's still trying to show the parameters of a bracket,

311
00:18:58,225 --> 00:19:02,390
then there's a little bit of a higher risk pre-empting that little bracket.

312
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,322
So, what we then need to do

313
00:19:04,322 --> 00:19:06,530
is we need to wait and allow the

314
00:19:06,530 --> 00:19:12,050
market to show us its hands, show us that actually it does want to bracket before we start initiating trades.

315
00:19:12,050 --> 00:19:13,749
So, that's all I'm trying to

316
00:19:13,749 --> 00:19:16,015
illustrate is the difference in odds or the

317
00:19:16,015 --> 00:19:18,281
difference in risk that you're taking when you're

318
00:19:18,281 --> 00:19:24,229
looking at a market that is bracketed already or when a market is looking to form some form of a bracket.

319
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:28,370
So, just understand that very important difference between the two.

320
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:35,170
Let's now go and have a look at a chart of what bracketing and trending would look like put together.

321
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:42,050
So, the example we've used is basically, in an upward auction,

322
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:48,180
we assess whether higher prices are cutting off activity or creating increased interest.

323
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:49,310
Now, remember what I said to you.

324
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:52,650
The objective of any market is to facilitate a trade.

325
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:57,075
So, when prices move higher, is it bringing in new business?

326
00:19:57,075 --> 00:20:01,030
In other words, is it saying, you know, more buyers need to come in and initiate?

327
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:05,690
Or is it getting responsive sellers into the market?

328
00:20:05,690 --> 00:20:08,379
And that's the question you have to answer

329
00:20:08,379 --> 00:20:11,068
yourself because if it's facilitating new business, there's

330
00:20:11,068 --> 00:20:15,438
a high probability that we're going to get strong initiative and momentum continuation.

331
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:18,045
Whereas if it's cutting off activity,

332
00:20:18,045 --> 00:20:21,845
it's likely we're going to get some form of reversion-type opportunity.

333
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:29,030
So, if high prices are increasing the bidding, so more buyers coming in, the risk of being long is low.

334
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:33,115
If short, the odds of suffering a loss are greatly increased.

335
00:20:33,115 --> 00:20:37,889
So, again, just coming back to that concept of just knowing whether

336
00:20:37,889 --> 00:20:41,072
or not we're bracketing or trending can increase

337
00:20:41,072 --> 00:20:45,448
or decrease the odds of success and, obviously, compounding potential losses.

338
00:20:45,450 --> 00:20:47,075
So, that's important to understand.

339
00:20:47,075 --> 00:20:53,080
That's why we spend quite a bit of time understanding the principle and the premise behind bracketing and trending markets.

340
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,930
So, what you've got is the example here.

341
00:20:54,930 --> 00:20:56,145
It's a candlestick chart.

