00:26:02,681 --> 00:26:06,593
can use to observe and identify potential turning points.

432
00:26:06,595 --> 00:26:11,055
We will develop these strategies also further on the blackboard later on.

433
00:26:11,055 --> 00:26:13,510
So, let's go through them one by one.

434
00:26:13,510 --> 00:26:15,497
So, there are two methods, but

435
00:26:15,497 --> 00:26:18,147
three examples that we're going to talk about

436
00:26:18,147 --> 00:26:22,453
when we talk about potential turning points from a trend back into bracketing.

437
00:26:22,455 --> 00:26:27,090
Now, the first one is the less frequent one, which is a loss of momentum.

438
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:32,270
So, almost like, you know, we have a flurry of force, some very strong initiative buying,

439
00:26:32,270 --> 00:26:37,260
and all of a sudden, you know, prices are moving higher and higher and advertising higher and higher prices.

440
00:26:37,260 --> 00:26:42,630
All of a sudden, there's just a real lack of interest to show initiative at higher prices.

441
00:26:42,630 --> 00:26:45,113
So, it's not to say that buyers don't want to

442
00:26:45,113 --> 00:26:48,589
be long. It's just that they don't want to show initiative at higher prices.

443
00:26:48,590 --> 00:26:54,460
Now, at this point, volume simply dries up or the lack of interest in a new business dries up.

444
00:26:54,460 --> 00:27:00,110
Now, we need that new business in order to continue to see the market initiating at higher prices.

445
00:27:00,110 --> 00:27:05,670
So, if everyone is fully committed and no one is left to participate, well, then it's very simple.

446
00:27:05,670 --> 00:27:10,470
There's a lot of, you know, you'll have, obviously, the initial longs that bought at the beginning of the trend.

447
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:13,450
You'll have more longs that bought sort of in the mature phase.

448
00:27:13,450 --> 00:27:16,067
And then, you'll have some weaker longs that bought sort

449
00:27:16,067 --> 00:27:17,899
of at the back end of the

450
00:27:17,899 --> 00:27:22,349
trend. And those weaker longs are likely to be the first ones that will liquidate those longs.

451
00:27:22,350 --> 00:27:24,490
And then we ultimately start bracketing.

452
00:27:24,490 --> 00:27:27,291
So this is the first sort of, you

453
00:27:27,291 --> 00:27:32,894
know, example that we will talk about when we talk about potential reversals in the market.

454
00:27:32,895 --> 00:27:37,505
And I'm going to show you examples and how they look in the volume profiles in the slides ahead.

455
00:27:37,505 --> 00:27:40,795
The next example is what we call an excess top.

456
00:27:40,795 --> 00:27:43,940
Again, this is probably the most frequent kind of top.

457
00:27:43,940 --> 00:27:47,424
As I would have spoken to you about in module one, this

458
00:27:47,424 --> 00:27:50,908
is the kind of top where we see a tail in the

459
00:27:50,908 --> 00:27:54,101
market or we almost see the market goes from initiative it

460
00:27:54,101 --> 00:28:01,069
runs into responsive other time frame players and then quickly backs off as prices are being advertised at either a discount or a premium.

461
00:28:02,110 --> 00:28:06,175
So the market makes a dramatic move higher or lower. So that's the initiative.

462
00:28:06,175 --> 00:28:11,165
